{%- comment -%}
  CallToolResult for arguments that fail the tool's input_schema (spec §10). Since MCP
  2025-11-25 (SEP-1303) input validation errors are tool execution errors, not protocol
  errors, so the model sees them and can correct its call. Shared by the inline
  tools/call path and approval/execute so both answer the same. Pure — no side effects.

  structuredContent carries the errors only when the tool declares no output_schema:
  a client may check structuredContent against the advertised outputSchema, which an
  error object would not match. The text content always carries them.

  @param {array}  errors - validate/json_schema errors (argument-shape facts only)
  @param {object} tool   - the resolved manifest
  @return {object} { content:[text], isError:true, structuredContent?:{validation_errors} }
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign joined = errors | join: '; '
  assign text = 'Invalid arguments: ' | append: joined
  assign item = {
    "type": "text",
    "text": text
  }
  assign content = []
  assign content = content | array_add: item

  assign sc = { "validation_errors": errors }

  assign result = {
    "content": content,
    "isError": true
  }
  if tool.output_schema == blank
    assign result['structuredContent'] = sc
  endif
  return result
%}
